PuTTY is the easiest, especially from someone who is habituated to the
Windows GUI style. Aside from a competant user interface, it has
excellent terminal emulation, a better VT100 than many if not all of
the commercial versions I've used.

Another option is to download cygwin and use the Win32 native version
of rxvt, which gives you a nice xterm-style terminal window without
forcing you to run X11. Make sure you also get the ssh package for
cygwin. Then you can start an rxvt, and run ssh to your chosen devnull
server.

PuTTY is at http://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/putty/
cygwin is at http://cygwin.com/

